        <obo:IAO_0000115>The protruding lymphoid tissue located on the mucosa of the intestine that is composed of densely packed B cell follicles.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002161 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_8459"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>Reptiles have accumulations of lymphocytes in their guts that may be primitive Peyer&apos;s patches (Zapata and Solas).</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>FMA has [set of?] [aggregated,small] lymphoid [follice,nodule] of [colon, SI, I, etc]</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>Pp is a syn for Aggregated lymphoid follicle of small intestine; but MA uses Pp as covering both SI and LI. MA also includes follicle as a part. WP says duodenum and jejunum lack PPs</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BTO:0001784</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
