        <obo:IAO_0000115>The great saphenous vein (GSV), also greater saphenous vein, is the large (subcutaneous) superficial vein of the leg and thigh. The terms &apos;safaina&apos; (Greek) and &apos;el safin&apos; (Arabic) have both been claimed as the origin for the word &apos;saphenous&apos;. [WP,unvetted].</obo:IAO_0000115>
