    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001485 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001485">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003840"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0011139"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001465"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The knee joint joins the thigh with the leg and consists of two articulations: one between the femur and tibia, and one between the femur and patella. It is the largest and most complicated joint in the human body. The knee is a mobile trocho-ginglymus (i.e. a pivotal hinge joint), which permits flexion and extension as well as a slight medial and lateral rotation[WP,unvetted].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EFO:0001957</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:19137</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:35175</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GAID:114</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
