        <owl:annotatedTarget>One of 3 small bones contained within the middle ear space and serve to transmit sounds from the air to the fluid-filled labyrinth. The absence of the auditory ossicles would constitute a moderate-to-severe hearing loss. The term &apos;ossicles&apos; literally means &apos;tiny bones&apos; and commonly refers to the auditory ossicles, though the term may refer to any small bone throughout the body. [WP,unvetted].</owl:annotatedTarget>
