    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001913 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001913">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0006314"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0006539"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An emulsion of fat globules within a fluid that is secreted by the mammary gland during lactation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>to axiomatize the different forms of mammary gland secretion an ontology of the phases of pregnancy/lactation is required. Using the existing GO def of lactation is circular.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>The detailed similarities of mammary glands in living monotremes, marsupials, and eutherians argue for a monophyletic origin of these glands, perhaps by the combination of parts of preexisting sebaceous and sweat glands.[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>ncit:Milk refers specifically to cow milk</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
