        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>The auditory hair cells in tetrapods are located in the inner ear in a structure known as the basilar papilla. In mammals this structure (along with some related structure) is called the organ of Corti.[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>in basal early lizards, organized into 3 tonotopically organized areas, the outer areas lack a tectorial membrane[ISBN:9780387714691]</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
