        <obo:IAO_0000115>The cavernous sinus (or lateral sellar compartment), within the human head, is a large collection of thin-walled veins creating a cavity bordered by the temporal bone of the skull and the sphenoid bone, lateral to the sella turcica.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>An irregularly shaped venous space in the dura mater at either side of the sphenoid bone[MESH:A07.231.908.224.334].</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
