            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A branch of the vagus nerve that supplies motor function and sensation to the larynx (voice box). It travels within the endoneurium. It is the nerve of the 6th Branchial Arch.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>Branch of the vagus nerve that separates from the vagus well postcranially, then continues anteriorly to innervate the larynx[AAO:0010754].</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>recurrent nerve</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>AAO:0010754</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
