        <obo:IAO_0000115>Mesenchyme enclosed by a dental organ that gives rise to an odontogenic papilla.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>we follow ZFA in introducing an additional distinction between the dental papilla and the (uncondensed) mesenchyme. Note that in some species such as zebrafish teeth are not part of the mouth, and sharks have dermal denticles which share similar developmental origins with teeth. For now we assume a NC origin for all and add a taxon restriction to 1st arch mesenchyme</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>Mesenchyme enclosed by dental organ.[MP]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
