        <obo:IAO_0000115>Anatomical system that has as its parts the organs concerned with the production and excretion of urine and those concerned with reproduction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>Anatomical system that has as its parts the organs concerned with the production and excretion of urine and those concerned with reproduction.[AAO]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000002>relationship type change: differentiates_from intermediate mesoderm (AAO:0010575) CHANGED TO: develops_from intermediate mesoderm (UBERON:0003064)[AAO]</obo:UBPROP_0000002>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>Kidneys and gonads (of vertebrates) develop from adjacent tissues, and after the excretory or urinary ducts have developed, the reproductive system usually taps into them or their derivatives.[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
