            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Subdivision of vertebral column that corresponds to the caudal subdivision of the body, containing the caudal vertebrae.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>Region of the vertebral column posterior to the caudal-sacral region, that may consists of two or three to more than 100 vertebrae. These vertebrae exhibit a gradual reduction in the sizes of their transverse processes and zygapophyses, but these structures are never entirely absent. All caudal vertebrae bear haemal arches.[AAO]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>in AAO, this is posterior to the caudal-sacral region</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>AAO:0000082</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:18043</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
