        <obo:IAO_0000115>A glandular epithelium that lines the stomach. The stomach&apos;s glandular epithelium is characterized by the presence of gastric glands.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>we follow Kardong in treating the glandular epithelium as a distinct entity, and thus as an epithelium which has glands; FMA has &apos;epithelium of gastric gland&apos;, which is part of the gastric gland.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:35814</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:63458</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MA:0002784</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>epithelium of gastric gland</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>gastric gland epithelium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
