    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0007195 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0007195">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003891"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002371"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003891"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002371"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The stroma of the bone marrow is all tissue not directly involved in the primary function of hematopoiesis. The yellow bone marrow belongs here, and makes the majority of the bone marrow stroma, in addition to stromal cells located in the red bone marrow. Yellow bone marrow is found in the Medullary cavity. Still, the stroma is indirectly involved in hematopoiesis, since it provides the hematopoietic microenvironment that facilitates hematopoiesis by the parenchymal cells. For instance, they generate colony stimulating factors, affecting hematopoiesis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CALOHA:TS-0085</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:21426</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Bone_marrow#Stroma</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>bone marrow stroma</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0007195</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#human_subset"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#mouse_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label>stroma of bone marrow</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0007195"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The stroma of the bone marrow is all tissue not directly involved in the primary function of hematopoiesis. The yellow bone marrow belongs here, and makes the majority of the bone marrow stroma, in addition to stromal cells located in the red bone marrow. Yellow bone marrow is found in the Medullary cavity. Still, the stroma is indirectly involved in hematopoiesis, since it provides the hematopoietic microenvironment that facilitates hematopoiesis by the parenchymal cells. For instance, they generate colony stimulating factors, affecting hematopoiesis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Bone_marrow#Stroma</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
