        <owl:annotatedTarget>The interphalangeal articulations of hand are hinge-joints of the phalanges of the hand. There are two sets (except in the thumb): &apos;proximal interphalangeal joints&apos; (PIP), those between the first (also called proximal) and second (intermediate) phalanges &apos;distal interphalangeal joints&apos; (DIP), those between the second and third (distal) phalanges A similar group of articulations also function in the toes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
