            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Layer of the entorhinal cortex that is most superficial, continuous with layer 1 of adjacent neocortex and the molecular layer of the subiculum, lying deep to the pial layer and superficial to layer 2. It is relatively acellular consisting mostly of fibers running transversely relative to the cortical surface (Adapted from Paxinos, G. The rat central nervous system, 2nd ed, Academic Press, San Diego, 1995, pg. 474).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>the two NIFSTD classes appear to refer to the same structure[DOI:10.1155/2008/381243]</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NLXANAT:090820</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NLXANAT:20090701</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>molecular layer of entorhinal cortex</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>superficial plexiform layer of entorhinal cortex</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EC layer 1</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>entorhinal cortex layer I</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>entorhinal cortex molecular layer</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>layer I of entorhinal cortex</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0022336</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#defined_by_cytoarchitecture"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#human_subset"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#mouse_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label>entorhinal cortex layer 1</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
